# The platform evidence already in the store, and what has been derived from it.
#
# Two kinds of evidence, both of them facts a harvester wrote and neither of
# them reachable by a facet:
#
#   - pu:operatingSystem on a package file, which the Open Audio Stack manifest
#     states for 559 plugins — "win", "mac", "linux".
#   - the download URL, whose filename is how a GitHub release says the same
#     thing: dm-BigMuff-windows.zip, master_me-1.3.1-macos-universal.dmg.
#
# Both are three blank nodes below the plugin, which is why neither could be
# filtered on. `src/harvest/Platforms.js` turns them into pu:Platform
# individuals; this only fetches them, so that the classifier is one function
# rather than a second copy written in SPARQL.
#
# ?derived comes back too, so the backfill can tell a plugin that needs writing
# from one already written and be a no-op on a second run.
#
# The graph is on every row because a write stays inside the graph the fact came
# from — a source's graph is a source's graph.
SELECT ?graph ?plugin ?system ?url ?derived
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?graph {
    ?plugin a trn:PluginProfile .
    OPTIONAL {
      ?plugin pu:package/pu:packageFile ?file .
      OPTIONAL { ?file pu:operatingSystem ?system }
      OPTIONAL { ?file pu:downloadUrl ?url }
    }
    OPTIONAL { ?plugin pu:supportedPlatform ?derived }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?graph ?plugin
